{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T22:53:41.592Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d97cc75851de74b9275ff63","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-8s53lj","claim:pm-hka7ep","claim:pm-wsqxwb","lineage:pm-wsqxwb","lineage:pm-5k4v","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-8s53lj+pm-hka7ep+pm-wsqxwb","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-8s53lj","claim:pm-hka7ep","claim:pm-wsqxwb","lineage:pm-wsqxwb","lineage:pm-5k4v","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-07T22:53:41.592Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reproduced on 2026.11.7 through the MCP tools/call handler (PM_MCP_PROFILE=full sandbox). pm_comments/pm_notes/pm_learnings with top-level add or text, and pm_files/pm_docs with top-level add, all returned an empty listing with success and wrote nothing. text was dead even nested (options.text), because the SDK only reads add. Only options.add wrote.\n\nFix (src/sdk/runtime-input.ts): CONTRACT_HOISTED_ACTIONS now covers comments, notes, learnings, files, docs and test beside the five read actions (pm_test with a flat add had the same silent read). declaredContractActionOptionKeys hoists every optional parameter PM_TOOL_ACTION_PARAMETER_CONTRACTS declares for them, excluding the operands id, text, query and keywords. Nested options still win. foldAnnotationTextOperand binds the annotation text operand (flat or nested) to add the way the CLI binds positional text. Equal values are accepted, and text that disagrees with add is refused with annotation_text_source_conflict before any write. The hoisted set also fixes flat limit, message, author, force, full, expectAt and the files lookupPath/discover parameters.\n\nParity spec tests/unit/mcp/annotation-tool-flat-parameters.spec.ts iterates the schema-declared keys of all six actions rather than a hand list. It also drives the tools/call path for each action with top-level add and text, then reads the written state back through the CLI.\n\nA census of the remaining actions found further silent drops outside this family (pm_history with a flat limit of 1 returns 10 entries), filed as pm-yjjo4l with a generic parity-harness AC instead of widening this batch.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T22:53:41.592Z"}],"before_hash":"26ad31f54b79a6e286b32f4ae14db64980b1102d357008e403426a699d654346","after_hash":"b09e9b4da1ce80226eee454e357bb30f938867e9aec37e58ad42f02d6de3ae96","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5defbf6d99c66a1956bf2b3853054a9153cccba2b575378a4b35692126ee72f8"}
